<div>
  <p>You can change the URL of your product by editing the gray text under the product description on the edit page. For example, you can change:</p>
  <p></p>
  <p>annagreen.gumroad.com/l/<b>QaSmj </b></p>
  <p>to </p>
  <p>annagreen.gumroad.com/l/<b>poetryclub</b></p>
  <figure><%= image_tag "https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/zljKufCmS0GdSXxRzz6mGOQOZoOhigO6TMfJ9CedSNEbuT8dWdR3oPhfVQrMdQFsW1y9APs2oo0efK32s1t1a2f889yfpIjCwKRV5KuvSoNHKetRI0km11Fwu6NbEvE7kp1YOfXbF2HjMLEU5ftz63M", width: 503, height: 448 %></figure>
  <br>
  <p>You can update this link at any time, but your previous custom URL will <span>not</span> redirect to the new custom URL. </p>
  <p>Your default Gumroad product link (annagreen.gumroad.com/l/QaSmj in this case) will continue to work as well.</p>
  <h3 id="What-you-can-put-in-a-custom-URL-fT7bQ">What you can put in a custom URL</h3>
  <p>A custom URL can contain letters, numbers, dashes, and underscores, and can be up to 255 characters long. The field drops anything else as you type, so if a character disappears while you are typing it is not allowed.</p>
  <p>Each of your products needs its own custom URL. If you try to reuse one you have already given to another of your products, you will see <i>"Custom permalink is already used by another one of your products"</i> when you save. Adding a word or a number is usually enough to make it unique.</p>
  <p>Products with license keys that were created before January 9, 2023 have one extra rule: their custom URL also has to be unused by every other Gumroad account, because license keys from before that date are looked up by the URL alone. If another account already holds it, you will see <i>"Custom permalink is in use by another Gumroad account, so it can't be used for a product with license keys. Pick a different one."</i> You cannot claim a URL another account is using, so choose something else.</p>
